 status←FetchAndStoreReadme packagePath;cfg;projectUrl;version;packageName;sourceUrl;refKind;markdown;qdmx
⍝ Fetches the README for the package in `packagePath` and records the outcome; see
⍝ `GetReadmeFilenames` for where it goes. Returns 'ok', 'none' or 'error'.
⍝ A package without a "project_url" - the field arrived after packages had been published -
⍝ yields 'none', which is the truth: there is nowhere to look.
⍝ Every outcome is recorded, 'error' included, so that the attempt is counted and the same
⍝ package is not picked again on the very next housekeeping run; `ReadmeIsDue` decides when
⍝ it comes round again. Nothing is recorded only when the package config itself cannot be
⍝ read, which says nothing about the README either way.
 status←'error'
⍝ Only the ways a config file can genuinely be unusable are trapped: 11 for JSON that will
⍝ not parse, 19 and 22 for no access and no file, and Tatin's own error number. A typo in
⍝ this code raises a VALUE ERROR, and that must reach the surface rather than vanish here.
 :Trap 11 19 22 Reg.ErrorNo
     cfg←Reg.GetPackageConfigFileAsNS packagePath
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     LogError'Cannot read the package config in "',packagePath,'": ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
     :Return
 :EndTrap
 projectUrl←{0=cfg.⎕NC ⍵:'' ⋄ cfg⍎⍵}'project_url'
 version←{0=cfg.⎕NC ⍵:'' ⋄ cfg⍎⍵}'version'
 packageName←{0=cfg.⎕NC ⍵:'' ⋄ cfg⍎⍵}'name'
 (status sourceUrl refKind markdown)←FetchReadme projectUrl version packageName
 StoreReadme packagePath status sourceUrl refKind markdown
⍝Done
